## WHAT k3s IS

k3s is a fully compliant Kubernetes distribution that packages the following into a single binary:
  - containerd (CRI runtime)
  - Flannel (CNI — VXLAN by default, wireguard-native for encrypted)
  - CoreDNS (cluster DNS)
  - Traefik v3 (ingress controller, since k3s v1.32; v2 on v1.21–v1.31)
  - ServiceLB / Klipper (LoadBalancer controller — bare-metal without cloud provider)
  - Kube-router netpol (network policy, embedded)
  - Local-path-provisioner (default StorageClass: local-path)
  - Spegel (distributed container image registry mirror)
  - Metrics-server (enables metrics.k8s.io API)
  - Helm Controller (manages HelmChart CRs)

k3s replaces heavy etcd with SQLite by default on single-server setups. For HA, use embedded etcd (3+ servers) or an external datastore (MySQL, PostgreSQL).

Server node: runs k3s server — control plane + datastore + kubelet + CNI
Agent node:  runs k3s agent  — kubelet + CNI only, no control plane
Both run containerd and the CNI. API server listens on port 6443.

