## CLUSTER ACCESS & AUTHENTICATION

### Admin kubeconfig
Written automatically to: /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml
Grants access as system:admin in system:masters group — unrestricted.
Certificates in this file are auto-rotated every time k3s starts.
If you copy this file elsewhere, you must manually update it when certs rotate.

To use externally:
  export KUBECONFIG=/etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml
  kubectl get pods --all-namespaces

To use from outside the cluster:
  Copy /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml to ~/.kube/config on your client machine.
  Replace "server: https://127.0.0.1:6443" with the actual server IP or hostname.

### Bearer Token Auth (PREFERRED for automation)
Header: Authorization: Bearer <token>

Token sources (k3s preference order):
  1. Admin token from kubeconfig:
       grep 'token:' /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml | awk '{print $2}'
  2. Short-lived projected ServiceAccount token (Kubernetes 1.21+):
       kubectl -n <namespace> create token <sa-name> --duration=86400s
  3. Long-lived SA secret token (explicitly created):
       kubectl -n <ns> get secret <sa-secret> -o jsonpath='{.data.token}' | base64 -d

### From inside a Pod (ServiceAccount auto-mount)
  Token: /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token
  CA:    /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/ca.crt
  API:   https://kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local

  TOKEN=$(cat /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token)
  curl --cacert /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/ca.crt \
       -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
       https://kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local/api/v1/namespaces

### API server addresses
  External (from outside): https://{{K3S_HOST}}:6443
  Internal (from pod):     https://kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local

### Standard curl pattern
  curl -k \
       -H "Authorization: Bearer {{K3S_TOKEN}}" \
       -H "Accept: application/json" \
       https://{{K3S_HOST}}:6443/<path>

  -k skips TLS verification — appropriate for homelab self-signed certs.
  Flag this if context suggests a production cluster.

