## PATCH TYPES — CHOOSE CAREFULLY

Content-Type header determines merge behavior:

  application/strategic-merge-patch+json  ← DEFAULT CHOICE for most resources
    Merges arrays by merge key (containers[] merged by .name).
    Safe for partial updates — won't wipe unmentioned fields.
    Example: update one env var without touching the rest of spec.

  application/merge-patch+json  (RFC 7396)
    Arrays are REPLACED entirely. Wipes containers[] if you only specify one.
    Use only when you intend a full array replacement.

  application/json-patch+json  (RFC 6902)
    Explicit operations: add, remove, replace, copy, move, test.
    Surgical precision. Best for single-field changes.

Common patch recipes:

  Scale deployment (strategic-merge):
    PATCH /apis/apps/v1/namespaces/{ns}/deployments/{name}
    {"spec":{"replicas":3}}

  Rolling restart (strategic-merge — add annotation to pod template):
    PATCH /apis/apps/v1/namespaces/{ns}/deployments/{name}
    {"spec":{"template":{"metadata":{"annotations":{"kubectl.kubernetes.io/restartedAt":"2026-03-13T00:00:00Z"}}}}}

  Update single container image (json-patch):
    PATCH /apis/apps/v1/namespaces/{ns}/deployments/{name}
    [{"op":"replace","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/image","value":"myimage:v2"}]

  Add label to pod (strategic-merge):
    PATCH /api/v1/namespaces/{ns}/pods/{name}
    {"metadata":{"labels":{"fabric/tier":"worker"}}}

