## RBAC MODEL

Every API call checks: (user or serviceaccount) has (verb) on (resource) in (namespace or cluster)

Verbs map to HTTP:
  get, list, watch → GET
  create           → POST
  update           → PUT
  patch            → PATCH
  delete           → DELETE
  exec, portforward → GET on subresource (requires separate RBAC entry)

Built-in ClusterRoles:
  cluster-admin    — full access (⚠ never bind to automation SAs)
  admin            — full access within a namespace
  edit             — read/write most resources, no RBAC management
  view             — read-only

Check permissions (SubjectAccessReview):
  POST /apis/authorization.k8s.io/v1/subjectaccessreviews
  {
    "apiVersion": "authorization.k8s.io/v1",
    "kind": "SubjectAccessReview",
    "spec": {
      "user": "system:serviceaccount:fabric:git-steer",
      "resourceAttributes": {
        "namespace": "default",
        "verb": "patch",
        "resource": "deployments",
        "group": "apps"
      }
    }
  }
  Check response: .status.allowed = true/false, .status.reason

