## k3s-SPECIFIC KNOWLEDGE

### Key file paths on a k3s server node
  /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml              — Admin kubeconfig (token + CA, auto-rotated on restart)
  /etc/rancher/k3s/config.yaml           — k3s server config (CLI flags as YAML)
  /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/token      — Node join token (K3S_TOKEN)
  /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/tls/       — All TLS certs
  /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/manifests/ — Auto-deploy: drop YAML here → applied on startup
  /var/lib/rancher/k3s/storage/          — local-path provisioner PV data (node-local)
  journalctl -u k3s                      — Server logs
  journalctl -u k3s-agent                — Agent logs

### Default networking (unless overridden in config.yaml)
  Pod CIDR:      10.42.0.0/16
  Service CIDR:  10.43.0.0/16
  DNS ClusterIP: 10.43.0.10
  CNI:           Flannel VXLAN
  Cluster domain: cluster.local
  For encryption: --flannel-backend=wireguard-native

### Flannel backends
  vxlan (default)       — UDP encapsulation, works across routed networks
  wireguard-native      — Encrypted, direct kernel WireGuard; replaces deprecated wireguard + ipsec backends
  host-gw               — IP routes via node IPs; requires L2 adjacency between all nodes
  none                  — Bring your own CNI (Cilium, Calico, Canal)

### ServiceLB (Klipper) — how LoadBalancer works without a cloud provider
  For each Service with type: LoadBalancer, k3s creates a DaemonSet in kube-system.
  DaemonSet spawns svc- prefixed pods that bind the host port using hostPort.
  Only deploys to nodes where the port is available.
  Node external IP → populated in service .status.loadBalancer.ingress[].ip
  Node internal IP → used if no external IP is configured.

  To restrict which nodes host LB pods:
    Label nodes: svccontroller.k3s.cattle.io/enablelb=true  (switches to allowlist mode)
    Pool routing: svccontroller.k3s.cattle.io/lbpool=pool1

  To disable ServiceLB (e.g. when installing MetalLB):
    Add --disable=servicelb to k3s server config

### Traefik
  Default IngressClass: "traefik"
  v3 since k3s v1.32 (upgraded from v2 automatically)
  LoadBalancer Service on ports 80 + 443 — uses ServiceLB by default
  All node IPs appear in Ingress .status unless ServiceLB node selection is restricted.
  Customize via HelmChartConfig in kube-system, NOT by editing traefik.yaml directly.

### Disabling bundled components
  --disable=traefik,coredns,servicelb,metrics-server,local-storage
  Or in /etc/rancher/k3s/config.yaml:
    disable:
      - traefik
      - servicelb

### HA configuration
  Embedded etcd (recommended): 3+ server nodes, --cluster-init on first server
  External DB: --datastore-endpoint="postgres://user:pass@host/dbname"
  SQLite: default for single server — not suitable for multi-server HA

### Node password secrets
  Stored in kube-system as <hostname>.node-password.k3s secrets
  If a node is removed and rejoined with same hostname, delete the old node + secret first.

