## STANDARD WORKFLOWS

### Cluster health snapshot
1. k8s_request GET /api/v1/nodes → all conditions Ready?
2. k8s_request GET /api/v1/namespaces/kube-system/pods → system pods healthy?
3. k8s_request GET /apis/metrics.k8s.io/v1beta1/nodes → CPU/memory pressure?
4. Report: N nodes, N/N ready | system pods N/N running | any warnings

### Debug a failing pod
1. k8s_request GET /api/v1/namespaces/{ns}/pods/{name}/status → phase, container states
2. k8s_request GET /api/v1/namespaces/{ns}/events?fieldSelector=involvedObject.name={name},type=Warning
3. k8s_logs tail 100 lines (add previous:true if container has restarted)
4. CrashLoopBackOff: check lastState.terminated.exitCode + reason
5. OOMKilled (137): suggest increasing memory limit in resources.limits.memory
6. Pending: check events for "Insufficient cpu/memory", "no nodes available", "unschedulable"
7. ImagePullBackOff: check image name, tag, and any imagePullSecrets

### Rolling restart a deployment
1. Confirm: "Confirm: rolling restart {name} in {ns}. All pods will cycle. Proceed?"
2. k8s_request PATCH strategic-merge:
   {"spec":{"template":{"metadata":{"annotations":{"kubectl.kubernetes.io/restartedAt":"<ISO8601 now>"}}}}}
3. Watch .status.availableReplicas until == .spec.replicas

### Scale a deployment
1. Confirm: "Confirm: scale {name} in {ns} to {n} replicas. Proceed?"
2. k8s_request PUT /apis/apps/v1/namespaces/{ns}/deployments/{name}/scale
   {"apiVersion":"autoscaling/v1","kind":"Scale","metadata":{"name":"{name}","namespace":"{ns}"},"spec":{"replicas":{n}}}

### Customize a bundled k3s component (e.g. Traefik)
1. k8s_request GET /apis/helm.cattle.io/v1/namespaces/kube-system/helmchartconfigs/traefik
   (check if one already exists)
2. k8s_apply dry_run:true with HelmChartConfig manifest in kube-system namespace, name: traefik
3. Confirm, apply
4. k3s will reconcile Traefik with new values automatically

### Create a least-privilege ServiceAccount
1. k8s_apply dry_run:true — ServiceAccount + Role with minimal verbs + RoleBinding
2. Confirm + apply
3. Create projected token: POST /api/v1/namespaces/{ns}/serviceaccounts/{name}/token
   {"apiVersion":"authentication.k8s.io/v1","kind":"TokenRequest","spec":{"expirationSeconds":86400}}
4. Return token once — remind user to store securely

### Check if a ServiceAccount has a specific permission
POST /apis/authorization.k8s.io/v1/subjectaccessreviews
user: "system:serviceaccount:{ns}:{name}"
resourceAttributes: {namespace, verb, resource, group}
Report .status.allowed + .status.reason

